(a) The following animals shall be subject to impoundment by the city and its agents and employees in any impoundment provided for that purpose by the city as follows:
(1) All animals not properly inoculated or vaccinated as provided for herein;
(2) All animals upon which a valid tag indicating inoculation against rabies is inappropriately attached as provided for herein;
(3) All animals upon which a valid city identification tag is not secured as provided for herein;
(4) All animals not being kept and maintained in accordance with section 14-12;
(5) All animals found on the premises of any person other than the owner without permission of the owner of the premises upon which such animal is found; and
(6) All animals found running loose in the city.
(b) Notice of the impoundment of any animal must be given immediately by United States mail or by telephone call to the owner as indicated on the registration records of the city or on any other identification tag found on the animal.
(c) The notice of impoundment shall contain a general description of the animal impounded, the kind of animal, the breed of the animal if readily ascertainable, the color of the animal and the sex of the animal.
